From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: don't read a dry cache with the film demuxed ahead

With 4K the demuxer runs far ahead of the picture: 73 s ahead when the
share went away in a test. The cache ran dry long before the queues did,
the next read waited on the source, and FFmpeg retries a stall for as
long as it lasts, so the player thread sat in that read for 75 s. The
underrun hold is decided on that thread, so it came only when the share
was back, after the queued minute had played out and the picture and
the sound had both run dry for three seconds.

Do not read while the cache is dry and more than a second is demuxed
ahead of the clock, in the audio as well as the video: the codec takes
tens of seconds of 4K video while the audio queue holds a few. Nothing is lost: what is queued plays on, the loop
keeps running, and the hold is taken once the queues run short, as 10
allows. Starts and seeks read as before: nothing is demuxed ahead there.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
@@ -1882,7 +1882,7 @@
     // Read nothing while buffering on a dry source: a read that stalls mid-element can
     // end demuxing until the next seek. The hold ends on the cache refilling, which is
     // measured without reading.
-    if (m_srcUnderrunHold)
+    if (m_srcUnderrunHold || SourceDryWithFilmAhead())
     {
       CThread::Sleep(10ms);
       continue;
@@ -2356,6 +2356,29 @@
   return info;
 }
 
+// A dry cache with the film demuxed well ahead is read for nothing: the read
+// waits on the source, and FFmpeg retries a stall for as long as it lasts, so the
+// player thread sat in one for 75 s while the queued minute played out, and the
+// hold, decided on that thread, came after the picture and the sound had run dry.
+// Nothing is lost by not reading: what is queued plays on, and the hold is taken
+// once it runs short.
+bool CVideoPlayer::SourceDryWithFilmAhead()
+{
+  const CacheInfo& cache = m_srcCache;
+  if (!cache.valid || cache.endCached || cache.endOfInput || cache.forwardTime < 0.0 ||
+      cache.forwardTime > SRC_EMPTY_TIME)
+    return false;
+
+  // Both runways: the video one can be tens of seconds while the audio's is gone.
+  const double clock = m_clock.GetClock();
+  const auto ahead = [clock](const CCurrentStream& stream)
+  {
+    return stream.id < 0 || (stream.dts != DVD_NOPTS_VALUE &&
+                             stream.dts - clock > DVD_SEC_TO_TIME(SRC_UNDERRUN_TIME));
+  };
+  return m_CurrentVideo.id >= 0 && ahead(m_CurrentVideo) && ahead(m_CurrentAudio);
+}
+
 bool CVideoPlayer::TryEnterSourceUnderrunHold()
 {
   if (m_pInputStream->IsRealtime() || m_pInputStream->IsEOF())
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.h
@@ -486,6 +486,7 @@
 
   double GetQueueTime();
   CacheInfo GetCachingTimes();
+  bool SourceDryWithFilmAhead();
 
   void FlushBuffers(double pts, bool accurate, bool sync);
 
